1‐Wire  bus  was originally developed by Dallas Semiconductor for
connecting integrated circuits.  It is commonly used for connect‐
ing devices such as electronic keys,  EEPROMs,  temperature  sen‐
sors, real‐time clocks, security chips, etc.  The driver provides
a  uniform programming interface layer between 1‐Wire master con‐
trollers and various 1‐Wire slave devices.   Each  1‐Wire  master
controller  attaches  a framework; several slave devices can then
be attached to the bus.  The driver supports plugging and unplug‐
ging slave devices on the fly.  1‐Wire  bus  bit‐banging  through
